      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Consider checking `capture_type \u003e\u003d 0` *before* casting it to `size_t` (i.e., `capture_type \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 static_cast\u003csize_t\u003e(capture_type) \u003c frame_sizes_.size()`). If `capture_type` is negative, casting it to `size_t` (an unsigned type) will wrap around to a very large positive number. While the current check technically works (because the large number will be `\u003e\u003d frame_sizes_.size()` and short-circuit), checking the lower bound before the unsigned cast makes the intent clearer and avoids the wrap-around. (Note that a similar check exists in `get_frame_size()`.)",
